results.description:
Quit porn. Reclaim who you are.

Paladin is the porn-recovery app for people who've outgrown the shame cycles, the faith-based programs, and the gimmicky streaks. No account. No cloud. No clinical language. Just a daily ritual, an identity you anchor to, and a rank system built for the long road.

// HOW IT WORKS
Open Paladin each morning. Tap I'M HERE TODAY if yesterday was clean — or log a slip if it wasn't. Under ten seconds. The streak builds. The rank advances. Badges accumulate. If you slip, the streak resets — but everything you've earned stays.

// TEN RANKS, RECRUIT TO HIGHLORD
Most apps stop counting at 90 days. Paladin's rank ladder runs Recruit → Squire → Knight → Vanguard → Captain → Commander → Marshal → Warden → Lord → Highlord. The top rank takes years. Because recovery is a decade, not a sprint.

// IDENTITY, NOT WILLPOWER
During onboarding, you write one line about who you're becoming. Paladin surfaces it at the moments that matter: the morning check-in, the panic flow, the milestones. The streak is real — but it's not the point. Who you said you'd be is the point.

// PANIC FLOW
When the urge hits, tap PANIC. Paladin walks you through a tactical interrupt — your reasons, your identity, your breath. Built for the actual moment, not the morning after.

// BLOCKING THAT ACTUALLY WORKS
Paladin skips the half-broken blocker. Instead, we walk you through Apple's native content filter and lock it with a passcode you can't quietly undo. About three minutes. Done right.

// PRIVACY BY DESIGN
No account. No login. No user IDs. Your data lives on your device and your private iCloud, end-to-end encrypted by Apple. App analytics are anonymous and EU-hosted — event counts only, nothing personal. We don't see your streak. We can't.

// SUBSCRIPTION
Three days free. One subscription after that. Cancel anytime in Settings. Your streak, your identity, your history are always yours — nothing gated, nothing held hostage.

// BUILT FOR THE LONG ROAD
Paladin is for people who've tried the other apps and want something that treats them like adults. Secular. Ceremonial. Anonymous. Built to open every morning, for years.

Subscriptions auto-renew unless canceled at least 24 hours before the period ends; manage or cancel any time in iOS Settings.

